-- 0101 — DRAFT-HYGIENE 2026-10-25 (owner order P1-4, approved for execution):
-- «أوقف إنشاء المسودات المكررة … ثم نفّذ تنظيفًا آمنًا للمسودات غير المطلوبة فقط»
--
-- WHAT THIS DOES (one-time, idempotent dedupe of EXISTING accumulation):
--   Deletes superseded duplicate AI-generated drafts — for every
--   (client_id, type) group of rows that are ALL:
--     status    = 'draft'          (never approved — no client ever saw it)
--     is_current= false            (never activated)
--     notes     = 'Generated by AI' (the runner's materialized rows only)
--   only the rows OLDER than the group's newest draft are removed; the
--   newest draft per group SURVIVES (it is the "completed-but-unsaved"
--   job the owner distinguished — still recoverable via the card).
--
-- WHAT THIS NEVER TOUCHES:
--   - approved / archived / is_current plans (any status ≠ 'draft')
--   - manually created drafts (notes ≠ 'Generated by AI')
--   - any other table (ai_jobs / plan_swaps / notifications untouched)
--
-- MEASURED BEFORE SHIPPING (read-only PostgREST, 2026-10-25):
--   3 AI drafts total; 1 duplicate group (client 87cd7ba6… type=meal,
--   drafts 4af96302 @21:30 + f038e77b @21:12) → exactly 1 row qualifies.
--
-- GOING FORWARD the mechanism itself is fixed in code (same commit):
--   the regeneration payload now carries replacePlanId and the runner
--   swaps the superseded draft out server-side, so no NEW duplicates
--   accumulate; this migration only clears the existing residue.
--
-- Idempotent: re-running is a no-op once deduped (no group keeps >1 row).

delete from public.plans as p
using public.plans as newer
where p.status = 'draft'
  and p.is_current = false
  and p.notes = 'Generated by AI'
  and newer.status = 'draft'
  and newer.is_current = false
  and newer.notes = 'Generated by AI'
  and newer.client_id = p.client_id
  and newer.type = p.type
  and newer.created_at > p.created_at;
